<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie and Tracking Statement — Aramo"
  description="The public Aramo Website sets no cookies and uses no analytics, advertising, telemetry, cross-site tracking, third-party embeds, social pixels, or third-party…"
  heading="Cookie and Tracking Statement"
>
  <p class="legal-note"><strong>Current posture</strong> The public Aramo Website sets no cookies and uses no analytics, advertising, telemetry, cross-site tracking, third-party embeds, social pixels, or third-party fonts. No cookie banner is currently presented because there are no cookies or tracking technologies for a visitor to accept or reject.</p>

  <h2>1. Technologies not used</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Essential or session cookies</li>
    <li>Preference or personalization cookies</li>
    <li>Analytics cookies or browser analytics</li>
    <li>Advertising cookies or pixels</li>
    <li>Cross-context behavioral advertising</li>
    <li>Social-media widgets or embeds</li>
    <li>Third-party content-delivery-network resources</li>
    <li>Device fingerprinting for advertising or analytics</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Server logs are not cookies</h2>
  <p>Our server records limited access-log information, including IP address, user agent, request, timestamp, and referrer. These logs are retained for 30 days for security and operations and then automatically deleted. They are not used for advertising or cross-site tracking.</p>

  <h2>3. Form anti-abuse controls</h2>
  <p>The form service temporarily uses IP addresses in memory to enforce request limits and uses a hidden field to filter bots. No persistent identifier is stored for the rate-limit function.</p>

  <h2>4. Future changes</h2>
  <p>Aramo will not deploy analytics, cookies, advertising technology, or other tracking on the public Website without first completing a legal and privacy review, updating the applicable notice, and implementing any required consent or opt-out controls.</p>
</LegalLayout>
